{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport inspect, aiter\nfor n in ['hipb_mm','rocb_mm','gemm_a16w16_asm','gemm_a16w16_opus','deepgemm','deepgemm_ck']:\n    obj=getattr(aiter,n,None)\n    print('\\\\n', n)\n    try:\n        print(inspect.signature(obj))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('signature err', type(e).__name__, e)\n    try:\n        print(inspect.getdoc(obj)[:1000] if inspect.getdoc(obj) else 'no doc')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('doc err', type(e).__name__, e)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport inspect, aiter\nfor n in ['hipb_mm','rocb_mm','gemm_a16w16_asm','gemm_a16w16_opus','deepgemm','deepgemm_ck']:\n    obj=getattr(aiter,n,None)\n    print('\\\\n', n)\n    try:\n        print(inspect.signature(obj))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('signature err', type(e).__name__, e)\n    try:\n        print(inspect.getdoc(obj)[:1000] if inspect.getdoc(obj) else 'no doc')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('doc err', type(e).__name__, e)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"[aiter] import [module_aiter_core] under /sgl-workspace/aiter/aiter/jit/module_aiter_core.so\n\n hipb_mm\n(*args, **kwargs)\nno doc\n\n rocb_mm\n(*args, **kwargs)\nno doc\n\n gemm_a16w16_asm\n(A: torch.Tensor, B: torch.Tensor, out: torch.Tensor, bias: torch.Tensor | None = None, splitK: int | None = None, kernelName: str | None = None, bpreshuffle: bool = False)\nno doc\n\n gemm_a16w16_opus\n(A: torch.Tensor, B: torch.Tensor, bias: torch.Tensor | None = None, dtype: torch.dtype = torch.bfloat16, *, kernelId: int | None = None, splitK: int | None = None, out: torch.Tensor | None = None) -> torch.Tensor\nShape-driven opus a16w16 GEMM.\n\nParameters\n----------\nA : [M, K] or [batch, M, K], bf16\nB : bf16 weight, plain layout (not pre-shuffled). Two accepted shapes:\n    * [N, K]            -- requires batch == 1 (i.e. A is 2D, or A is\n                           3D with leading dim 1).\n    * [batch, N, K]     -- contiguous strides (N*K, K, 1) only.\n                           Broadcast views (e.g. ``B.unsqueeze(0).\n                           expand(batch, -1, -1)``) are rejected\n                           because the opus launcher assumes\n                           ``stride_b_batch == N*K``; pass\n                           ``.contiguous()`` if you need to broadcast\n                           a single-batch weight across A.\nbias : optional per-output-feature b